    fix(v4): validate the address, and return the string that was validated (#6442)

    new URL("http://[" + value + "]") parses an authority, not an address, so `@` and `\` re-delimit it and the parser validates something else: z.ipv6().parse("::@1\\") passed against the host 0.0.0.1. Guard on the address alphabet instead, and let isValidCIDRv6 delegate to isValidIPv6.

